## Biographies
Yuyang Tian was born in 1984 in Liaoning, China. He received his B.Sc. in Material Chemistry from Jilin University in 2007 and Ph.D. in Chemistry from the University of St. Andrews in 2014. In 2015, he joined the faculty of Northeast Normal University, Changchun, China. He is currently an Associate Professor in the Key Laboratory of Polyoxometalate Science of Ministry of Education. His current research interests focus on the design, synthesis, and applications of functional porous aromatic frameworks.
Guangshan Zhu was born in 1971 in Henan, China. He received his B.Sc. (1993) and Ph.D. (1998) degrees in Chemistry from Jilin University. He was a Postdoctoral Fellow with Professor Osamu Terasaki at Tohoku University, Japan, in 1999−2000. He became a full Professor in Jilin University since 2001. In 2015, he moved to Northeast Normal University. He is the holder of the National Science Fund for Distinguished Young Scholars, Chang Jiang Scholars Program, Science and Technology Innovation Leader in Tenthousand Talents Program and Lu Jiaxi Excellent Tutor Award. His current research interest focuses on the design and synthesis of porous frameworks and porous framework membranes, driven by the demands in sustainable energy and environments such as adsorption, separation, and radioactive element capture. Now he has published over 370 research papers and his h-index is 65.
